  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Malaria control in Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Mali, malaria is endemic amongst more than 90 percent of the population. The overall goal of the program supported by this grant is to contribute to the reduction of illness and death linked to malaria in Mali. The main activity implemented in this grant comprises the acquisition and distribution of insecticide-treated nets to pregnant women and children under the age of 5 with the aim of significantly contributing to the reduction of malaria among these biologically vulnerable groups. Important behavioral community change activities are also being implemented to support the preventive component addressed by this grant.</narrative>
  </description>
